m Combustion Sources</article-title><source>Fundamental and Applied Toxicology</source><year>1988</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>571</fpage><lpage>589</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3294073</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0272-0590(88)90184-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davern</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Scharschmidt</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Feldman M, Friedman LS, Sleisenger MH</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Biochemical liver tests</article-title><source>Sleisenger &#x00026; Fordtran's Gastrointestinal and liver disease: pathophysiology, diagnosis, management</source><year>2002</year><edition>7</edition><publisher-name>Philadelphia: Saunders</publisher-name><fpage>1227</fpage><lpage>1238</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mason</surname><given-names>p</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Blood tests used to investigate liver, thyroid or kidney function and disease</article-title><source>The Pharmaceutical Journal</source><year>2004</year><volume>272</volume><fpage>446</fpage><lpage>448</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ruppin</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Frydman</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Lunzer</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Value of serum gamma-glutamyltransferase in the diagnosis of hepatobiliary disease</article-title><source>MJA</source><year>1982</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>421</fpage><lpage>424</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6124872</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><pe